{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to `ff578fef`, item 6 and its reason. The ruling stands.\nI named the wrong cause.\n\n1. The case is the ordinary race, and no fault of a replica.\n   Member A explores at head 39. The act of member B takes effect\n   at head 40 before the scope judges the request of A. The scope\n   refuses with `revision-moved`. The replica of A was current at\n   the submit.\n2. The member's path in that case: the draft returns with the\n   cause. The next submit explores, finds the moved basis, and\n   returns the draft with `now`. The submit after that signs. This\n   is one submit more than section 6 of the act environment note\n   promised. State it in the how-to page in these terms.\n3. The rule that pays for the extra submit: a draft changes only by\n   a call of the member. No background step writes to the draft\n   store. So two clients of one member never race to store a\n   return, and a stop between the custody write and a draft write\n   leaves nothing to repair.\n4. A second reason for form 2: an act that makes a new item has no\n   row. Its refusal has no `now` in any design.\n\nIf the plan shows that form 2 costs more than this, tell me before\nyou write source.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}